desc(
	mode: "source"
	language: "general"
	title: "Tls Renegotiation"
	title_zh: "Tls Renegotiation"
	type: vuln
	level: middle
	rule_id: "source-insecure-api-tls-renegotiation"
	risk: "Security"
	desc: <<<DESC
Migrated from Semgrep rule `tls-renegotiation` (problem-based-packs/insecure-transport/java-stdlib/tls-renegotiation.yaml).
Original message: Checks for cases where java applications are allowing unsafe renegotiation. This leaves the application vulnerable to a man-in-the-middle attack where chosen plain text is injected as prefix to a TLS connection.
CWE: CWE-319: Cleartext Transmission of Sensitive Information
References:
- https://www.oracle.com/java/technologies/javase/tlsreadme.html
Note: source-mode regex approximation of a safe-literal Semgrep pattern.
DESC
	solution: <<<SOLUTION
Review this occurrence and replace it with a safer alternative.
SOLUTION
	alert_min: 1
	"file://pos.java": <<<POS
java.lang.System.setProperty("sun.security.ssl.allowUnsafeRenegotiation", true);
POS
	"safefile://pos.java": <<<NEG
java.lang.System.setProperty("sun.security.ssl.allowUnsafeRenegotiation", false);
NEG
)

${*.java}.pattern_regex(/(?:java\.lang\.System\.setProperty\("sun\.security\.ssl\.allowUnsafeRenegotiation",\s+true\);)/) as $hit
alert $hit for {
	level: "middle",
	title: "Tls Renegotiation",
	title_zh: "Tls Renegotiation",
	message: "Tls Renegotiation detected.",
}
